/-!
# `BenzecriScaffold.Projective.Groups` — `GL`, `GA`, `GS`, `GU` and the isomorphism `i` (p. 236)

J.-P. Benzécri, *Sur les variétés localement affines et localement projectives*, Bull. SMF 88
(1960) 229–332, Chapter 1 § 1, journal p. 236 (unlabelled prose); transcription
`papers/benzecri/legacy/labeled/benzecri1960_ch1.tex:274–276` and `:294–302`. Package WP-45d
(wave 1, layer L1). The prose carries no ledger label, so nothing is marked; the groups are the
`G` of Déf. 12 (`bzdef:c1s1d12_variete_localement_projective`, `benzecri1960_ch1.tex:304`) and
their rigidity is what Prop. 1 (`bzprop:c1s1p1_cartes_compatibles`, `benzecri1960_ch1.tex:340`)
needs; neither label is certified here.

> Nous désignons par $GL(n, \R)$ le groupe des automorphismes de l'espace vectoriel $\R^n$; par
> $GA(n, \R)$ le groupe des automorphismes de la structure d'espace affin de $\R^n$ :
> $GA(n, \R)$ est engendré par $GL(n, \R)$ et par le groupe des translations. (l.274–276)
>
> Le quotient $GS(n-1, \R)$ de $GL(n, \R)$ par le sous-groupe des homothéties positives opère sur
> $S(n-1)$ : c'est le groupe des automorphismes de la structure projective de $S(n-1)$. De même,
> le quotient $GP(n-1, \R)$ de $GL(n, \R)$ par le sous-groupe de toutes les homothéties opère sur
> $P(n-1)$ et c'est le groupe des automorphismes de sa structure projective.
>
> $GL(n, \R)$ est le produit direct du sous-groupe, isomorphe à $\R^+$, des homothéties positives,
> et du sous-groupe, $GU(n, \R)$ des automorphismes de $\R^n$ dont le déterminant a pour valeur
> absolue 1; la projection de $GL(n, \R)$ sur son quotient $GS(n-1, \R)$ définit donc un
> isomorphisme (noté $i$) de $GS(n-1, \R)$ sur $GU(n, \R)$. (l.294–302)

## What is proved (no `sorry`)

Over an arbitrary real vector space `E` (`GL(E) = E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E`), and then at `E = ℝⁿ`:
* `Benzecri.posHomotheties E` (the positive homotheties, a normal — indeed central — subgroup),
  `Benzecri.GSE E = GL(E) ⧸ posHomotheties E`, its action on `Sphere E` (`Benzecri.GSE.mk_smul`);
* **rigidity**: an element of `GL(E)` fixing every point of a nonempty open set of `S(E)` is a
  positive homothety (`Benzecri.mem_posHomotheties_of_eqOn`), via the linear-algebra lemma
  `Benzecri.exists_forall_eq_smul_of_isOpen` (a linear map for which every vector of a nonempty
  open set is an eigenvector is a homothety); hence `IsAnalyticAction (GSE E) (Sphere E)`
  (faithful and rigid) and `IsRigidAction (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) (Sphere E)`, for every real topological
  vector space `E` with `{0}` closed;
* continuity: `ContinuousConstSMul (GSE E) (Sphere E)` in finite dimension;
* `Benzecri.GU E` (`|det| = 1`), `Benzecri.glEquivProd : GL(E) ≃* ℝ⁺ × GU(E)` (the direct product,
  `g ↦ (|det g|^{1/n}, |det g|^{-1/n} g)`), `Benzecri.posHomothetiesEquiv : ℝ⁺ ≃* posHomotheties E`,
  and **`Benzecri.isoGU : GSE E ≃* GU E`**, the paper's `i`, with `isoGU (mk g) = |det g|^{-1/n} g`
  (`Benzecri.isoGU_mk`), for `E` finite-dimensional and nonzero;
* `GA(n, ℝ)` (`Benzecri.GAR n`, Mathlib's `AffineEquiv`) is generated by `GL(n, ℝ)` and the
  translations (`Benzecri.closure_linear_union_translations`), each element being a translation
  after a linear automorphism (`Benzecri.GAR.eq_translation_mul_linear`), acting continuously
  (`Benzecri.GAR.continuous`); it is exactly the group of bijections of `ℝⁿ` affine in the sense of
  Déf. 2 (`Benzecri.GAR.isAffine`, `Benzecri.GAR.exists_eq_of_isAffine`).
* The paper's indexing: `GLR n = GL(n, ℝ)`, `GAR n = GA(n, ℝ)`, `GUR n = GU(n, ℝ)`,
  `GSR m = GS(m, ℝ) = GL(m+1, ℝ)/ℝ⁺` acting on `S m = S(ℝᵐ⁺¹)`, `isoGUR m : GSR m ≃* GUR (m+1)`.

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper hypothesis | here |
|---|---|
| `GL(n, ℝ)` acting on `ℝⁿ` | ⚠ weakened: any real vector space `E` (`E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E`) for the quotient, the action and rigidity |
| « opère sur $S(n-1)$ » (by homeomorphisms) | ✓ carried: `ContinuousConstSMul (GSE E) (Sphere E)`, `E` finite-dimensional |
| « produit direct … isomorphe à $\R^+$ » | ✓ carried, for `E ≠ 0` finite-dimensional (`n ≥ 1`: for `n = 0`, `GL(0)` is trivial and not `ℝ⁺ × GU(0)`; Benzécri's `S(n−1)`, `n ≥ 1`). Only the product decomposition `glEquivProd` needs `n ≥ 1`; `isoGU` carries `[Nontrivial E]` from its section, though at `E = 0` both sides are trivial |
| `GA(n, ℝ)`, « automorphismes de la structure d'espace affin » | ✓ carried as `AffineEquiv`, Déf. 2 in the linear reading of DEC-114 (`GAR.isAffine`, `GAR.exists_eq_of_isAffine`) |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

* « c'est le groupe des automorphismes de la structure projective de $S(n-1)$ » is not stated
  here: the projective structure is wave 2 (`Structure/Basic`). What is proved is the input it
  needs: the action is by homeomorphisms, faithful and rigid.
* `GP(n−1, ℝ)` and its action on `P(n−1)` are not formalized (named only; no use in Ch. 1).
* Continuity of the action is per element (`ContinuousConstSMul`); no topology on the groups.
* Naming: `GLR`, `GAR`, `GSR`, `GUR` (`R` for `ℝ`), because Mathlib's global notation `GL`
  (`Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup`) would capture an identifier `GL`.

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
-/

noncomputable section

open Set Topology

namespace Benzecri

/-! ### Positive homotheties and `GS(E) = GL(E)/ℝ⁺` -/

section Homotheties

variable (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E]

/-- The homothety of ratio `c ∈ ℝ*`, as a group homomorphism `ℝ* →* GL(E)`. -/
def homothety : ℝˣ →* (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) := DistribMulAction.toModuleAut ℝ E

@[simp] theorem homothety_apply (c : ℝˣ) (v : E) : homothety E c v = (c : ℝ) • v := rfl

/-- **The positive homotheties**, the image of `ℝ⁺ = Units.posSubgroup ℝ`. -/
def posHomotheties : Subgroup (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) := (Units.posSubgroup ℝ).map (homothety E)

variable {E}

theorem mem_posHomotheties {g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E} :
    g ∈ posHomotheties E ↔ ∃ c : ℝ, 0 < c ∧ ∀ v, g v = c • v := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨c, (Units.mem_posSubgroup c).1 hc, fun v => rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨c, hc, h⟩
    refine ⟨Units.mk0 c hc.ne', (Units.mem_posSubgroup _).2 hc, ?_⟩
    ext v
    simp [h]

theorem homothety_mul_comm (c : ℝˣ) (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) : homothety E c * g = g * homothety E c := by
  ext v
  simp [LinearEquiv.mul_apply]

/-- Positive homotheties are central, hence normal. -/
instance : (posHomotheties E).Normal := by
  refine ⟨fun h hh g => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩ := hh
  rw [← homothety_mul_comm c g, mul_inv_cancel_right]
  exact ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩

/-- A positive homothety acts trivially on `S(E)`. -/
theorem smul_eq_self_of_mem_posHomotheties {g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E} (hg : g ∈ posHomotheties E)
    (x : Sphere E) : g • x = x := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc, h⟩ := mem_posHomotheties.1 hg
  induction x using Sphere.ind with
  | h v hv =>
    rw [Sphere.smul_mk]
    simp_rw [h]
    exact Sphere.mk_smul hv hc _

variable (E) in
/-- **`GS(E) = GL(E)/ℝ⁺`** (p. 236, « Le quotient $GS(n-1, \R)$ de $GL(n, \R)$ par le sous-groupe
des homothéties positives »), for any real vector space `E`. -/
abbrev GSE : Type _ := (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) ⧸ posHomotheties E

variable (E) in
/-- The action of `GL(E)` on `S(E)` as a hom to permutations, trivial on `ℝ⁺`, descended to `GS`. -/
def GSE.toPerm : GSE E →* Equiv.Perm (Sphere E) :=
  QuotientGroup.lift (posHomotheties E) (MulAction.toPermHom (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) (Sphere E))
    fun _g hg => Equiv.ext fun x => smul_eq_self_of_mem_posHomotheties hg x

/-- **`GS(E)` acts on `S(E)`** (« opère sur $S(n-1)$ »). -/
instance : MulAction (GSE E) (Sphere E) := MulAction.compHom (Sphere E) (GSE.toPerm E)

@[simp] theorem GSE.mk_smul (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) (x : Sphere E) :
    (QuotientGroup.mk g : GSE E) • x = g • x := rfl

theorem GSE.smul_def (g : GSE E) (x : Sphere E) : g • x = GSE.toPerm E g x := rfl

/-- In finite dimension, `GS(E)` acts on `S(E)` by homeomorphisms. -/
instance [TopologicalSpace E] [IsTopologicalAddGroup E] [ContinuousSMul ℝ E] [T2Space E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] : ContinuousConstSMul (GSE E) (Sphere E) := by
  refine ⟨fun g => ?_⟩
  induction g using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
  | H g => exact Sphere.continuous_smul_linearEquiv g

end Homotheties

/-! ### Rigidity -/

section Rigidity

/-- **A linear map for which every vector of a nonempty open set is an eigenvector is a
homothety.** More precisely, if `g z ∈ ℝ z` for every `z` of an open `O ∋ x`, `x ≠ 0`, then
`g = c • id` with `g x = c • x`. -/
theorem exists_forall_eq_smul_of_isOpen {E : Type*} [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E]
    [TopologicalSpace E] [ContinuousAdd E] [ContinuousSMul ℝ E] (g : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) {O : Set E}
    (hO : IsOpen O) {x : E} (hxO : x ∈ O) (hx0 : x ≠ 0) (hg : ∀ z ∈ O, ∃ c : ℝ, g z = c • z) :
    ∃ c : ℝ, g x = c • x ∧ ∀ y, g y = c • y := by
  obtain ⟨c₀, hc₀⟩ := hg x hxO
  refine ⟨c₀, hc₀, fun y => ?_⟩
  by_cases hdep : ∃ a : ℝ, a • x = y
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hdep
    rw [map_smul, hc₀, smul_comm]
  have hli : LinearIndependent ℝ ![x, y] :=
    (LinearIndependent.pair_iff' hx0).2 fun a ha => hdep ⟨a, ha⟩
  have hcont : Continuous fun t : ℝ => x + t • y :=
    continuous_const.add (continuous_id.smul continuous_const)
  have hmem : (fun t : ℝ => x + t • y) ⁻¹' O ∈ 𝓝 (0 : ℝ) :=
    hcont.continuousAt.preimage_mem_nhds (by simpa using hO.mem_nhds hxO)
  obtain ⟨ε, hε, hball⟩ := Metric.mem_nhds_iff.1 hmem
  set t₁ : ℝ := ε / 2 with ht₁
  set t₂ : ℝ := ε / 4 with ht₂
  have h1 : x + t₁ • y ∈ O := hball (by
    rw [Metric.mem_ball, Real.dist_eq, sub_zero, abs_of_pos (by positivity)]; linarith)
  have h2 : x + t₂ • y ∈ O := hball (by
    rw [Metric.mem_ball, Real.dist_eq, sub_zero, abs_of_pos (by positivity)]; linarith)
  obtain ⟨c₁, hc₁⟩ := hg _ h1
  obtain ⟨c₂, hc₂⟩ := hg _ h2
  rw [map_add, map_smul, hc₀] at hc₁ hc₂
  -- `t₁ t₂ • g y` computed in two ways
  have e : ((t₂ * c₁ - t₂ * c₀) • x + (t₁ * t₂ * c₁) • y) =
      ((t₁ * c₂ - t₁ * c₀) • x + (t₁ * t₂ * c₂) • y) := by
    have e1 : (t₁ * t₂) • g y = (t₂ * c₁ - t₂ * c₀) • x + (t₁ * t₂ * c₁) • y := by
      have := congrArg (fun w => t₂ • w) hc₁
      simp only [smul_add, smul_smul] at this
      rw [mul_comm t₁ t₂, mul_comm t₂ c₁, mul_comm t₂ c₀, sub_smul]
      rw [mul_comm t₂ t₁] at this ⊢
      calc (t₁ * t₂) • g y = (t₂ * t₁) • g y := by rw [mul_comm]
        _ = _ := by
          rw [mul_comm t₂ t₁]
          linear_combination (norm := module) this
    have e2 : (t₁ * t₂) • g y = (t₁ * c₂ - t₁ * c₀) • x + (t₁ * t₂ * c₂) • y := by
      have := congrArg (fun w => t₁ • w) hc₂
      simp only [smul_add, smul_smul] at this
      linear_combination (norm := module) this
    rw [← e1, ← e2]
  obtain ⟨ha, hb⟩ := hli.eq_of_pair e
  have ht : t₁ * t₂ ≠ 0 := by positivity
  have hc12 : c₁ = c₂ := by
    have : t₁ * t₂ * (c₁ - c₂) = 0 := by linarith
    rcases mul_eq_zero.1 this with h | h
    · exact absurd h ht
    · linarith
  have hc10 : c₁ = c₀ := by
    subst hc12
    have : (t₂ - t₁) * (c₁ - c₀) = 0 := by linarith
    rcases mul_eq_zero.1 this with h | h
    · exfalso; rw [ht₁, ht₂] at h; linarith
    · linarith
  subst hc10
  have ht1 : t₁ ≠ 0 := by positivity
  have : t₁ • g y = t₁ • (c₁ • y) := by
    linear_combination (norm := module) hc₁
  exact smul_right_injective E ht1 this

variable {E : Type*} [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace E] [ContinuousAdd E]
  [ContinuousSMul ℝ E] [T1Space E]

/-- **Rigidity of the action of `GL(E)` on `S(E)`**: an automorphism fixing every point of a
nonempty open set of `S(E)` is a positive homothety. (`[T1Space E]` is used only through
`Sphere.isOpen_iff_F`; it is more than rigidity needs, and holds for every space Ch. 1 uses.) -/
theorem mem_posHomotheties_of_eqOn {g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E} {U : Set (Sphere E)} (hU : IsOpen U)
    (hne : U.Nonempty) (h : EqOn (fun p => g • p) id U) : g ∈ posHomotheties E := by
  have hFU : IsOpen (Sphere.F U) := Sphere.isOpen_iff_F.1 hU
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hne
  induction x using Sphere.ind with
  | h v hv =>
  have hvF : v ∈ Sphere.F U := ⟨hv, hx⟩
  have key : ∀ z ∈ Sphere.F U, ∃ c : ℝ, 0 < c ∧ g z = c • z := by
    rintro z ⟨hz, hzU⟩
    have := h hzU
    simp only [Sphere.smul_mk, id] at this
    obtain ⟨c, hc, hcz⟩ := (Sphere.mk_eq_mk_iff_exists_pos hz _).1 this.symm
    exact ⟨c, hc, hcz.symm⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hcv, hall⟩ := exists_forall_eq_smul_of_isOpen (g : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) hFU hvF hv
    fun z hz => let ⟨c, _, h⟩ := key z hz; ⟨c, h⟩
  obtain ⟨c', hc', hc'v⟩ := key v hvF
  have hcc : c = c' := by
    have : (c - c') • v = 0 := by
      rw [sub_smul]; exact sub_eq_zero.2 (hcv.symm.trans hc'v)
    exact sub_eq_zero.1 ((smul_eq_zero.1 this).resolve_right hv)
  exact mem_posHomotheties.2 ⟨c, hcc ▸ hc', hall⟩

/-- An automorphism acting trivially on all of `S(E)` is a positive homothety. -/
theorem mem_posHomotheties_of_forall_smul_eq {g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E} (h : ∀ p : Sphere E, g • p = p) :
    g ∈ posHomotheties E := by
  by_cases hE : Nontrivial E
  · obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_ne (0 : E)
    exact mem_posHomotheties_of_eqOn isOpen_univ ⟨Sphere.mk v hv, trivial⟩ fun p _ => h p
  · rw [not_nontrivial_iff_subsingleton] at hE
    exact mem_posHomotheties.2 ⟨1, one_pos, fun v => Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩

/-- **The action of `GS(E)` on `S(E)` is faithful and rigid** (`IsAnalyticAction`): an element of
`GS` agreeing with another on a nonempty open set is equal to it. -/
instance : IsAnalyticAction (GSE E) (Sphere E) where
  eq_of_smul_eq_smul {g h} hgh := by
    induction g using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
    | H g =>
    induction h using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
    | H h =>
    rw [QuotientGroup.eq]
    apply mem_posHomotheties_of_forall_smul_eq
    intro p
    have := hgh p
    simp only [GSE.mk_smul] at this
    rw [mul_smul, ← this, inv_smul_smul]
  smul_eq_of_eqOn {g h U} hU hne heq := by
    induction g using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
    | H g =>
    induction h using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
    | H h =>
    have hmem : h⁻¹ * g ∈ posHomotheties E := by
      refine mem_posHomotheties_of_eqOn hU hne fun p hp => ?_
      have := heq hp
      simp only [GSE.mk_smul] at this
      simp only [id, mul_smul, this, inv_smul_smul]
    intro p
    simp only [GSE.mk_smul]
    have := smul_eq_self_of_mem_posHomotheties hmem p
    rw [mul_smul, inv_smul_eq_iff] at this
    exact this

/-- The action of `GL(E)` itself on `S(E)` is rigid (not faithful: `ℝ⁺` acts trivially). -/
instance : IsRigidAction (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) (Sphere E) :=
  IsRigidAction.of_comp (G := GSE E) (QuotientGroup.mk' (posHomotheties E)) fun _ _ => rfl

/-- **Rigidity of `GS(E)`, one-element form**: an element of `GS(E)` fixing every point of a
nonempty open set of `S(E)` is the identity. -/
theorem GSE.eq_one_of_eqOn {g : GSE E} {U : Set (Sphere E)} (hU : IsOpen U) (hne : U.Nonempty)
    (h : EqOn (fun p => g • p) id U) : g = 1 :=
  eq_of_eqOn hU hne (fun p hp => by simpa using h hp)

end Rigidity

/-! ### `GU(E)`, the decomposition `GL = ℝ⁺ × GU`, and the isomorphism `i : GS ≃* GU` -/

section Unimodular

variable (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E]

/-- **`GU(E)`**: the automorphisms whose determinant has absolute value `1`. Meaningful for
finite-dimensional `E`: outside finite dimension `LinearEquiv.det` is the junk value `1`, so there
`GU E = ⊤`. -/
def GU : Subgroup (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) where
  carrier := {g | |((LinearEquiv.det g : ℝˣ) : ℝ)| = 1}
  mul_mem' {a b} ha hb := by
    simp only [mem_setOf_eq, map_mul, Units.val_mul, abs_mul] at *
    rw [ha, hb, one_mul]
  one_mem' := by simp
  inv_mem' {a} ha := by
    simp only [mem_setOf_eq, map_inv, Units.val_inv_eq_inv_val, abs_inv] at *
    rw [ha, inv_one]

variable {E}

theorem mem_GU {g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E} : g ∈ GU E ↔ |((LinearEquiv.det g : ℝˣ) : ℝ)| = 1 := Iff.rfl

theorem det_homothety [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (c : ℝˣ) :
    ((LinearEquiv.det (homothety E c) : ℝˣ) : ℝ) = (c : ℝ) ^ Module.finrank ℝ E := by
  rw [LinearEquiv.coe_det]
  have : ((homothety E c : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) = (c : ℝ) • LinearMap.id := by
    ext v; simp
  rw [this, LinearMap.det_smul, LinearMap.det_id, mul_one]

/-- `|det g| > 0`. -/
theorem absDet_pos (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) : 0 < |((LinearEquiv.det g : ℝˣ) : ℝ)| :=
  abs_pos.2 (LinearEquiv.det g).ne_zero

/-- The ratio `|det g|^{1/n}` of the homothety factor of `g` (`n = dim E`). -/
def homRatio (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) : ℝ :=
  |((LinearEquiv.det g : ℝˣ) : ℝ)| ^ ((Module.finrank ℝ E : ℝ)⁻¹)

theorem homRatio_pos (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) : 0 < homRatio g := Real.rpow_pos_of_pos (absDet_pos g) _

theorem homRatio_mul (g h : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) : homRatio (g * h) = homRatio g * homRatio h := by
  simp only [homRatio, map_mul, Units.val_mul, abs_mul]
  exact Real.mul_rpow (abs_nonneg _) (abs_nonneg _)

variable (E) in
/-- `g ↦ |det g|^{1/n} ∈ ℝ⁺`, a homomorphism. -/
def homRatioHom : (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) →* Units.posSubgroup ℝ where
  toFun g := ⟨Units.mk0 (homRatio g) (homRatio_pos g).ne', (Units.mem_posSubgroup _).2
    (homRatio_pos g)⟩
  map_one' := by
    ext; simp [homRatio]
  map_mul' g h := by
    ext; simp [homRatio_mul]

@[simp] theorem coe_homRatioHom (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) :
    (((homRatioHom E g : Units.posSubgroup ℝ) : ℝˣ) : ℝ) = homRatio g := rfl

/-- The `GU` part of `g`: `|det g|^{-1/n} g`. -/
def unitPart (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E := homothety E (homRatioHom E g : ℝˣ)⁻¹ * g

theorem unitPart_apply (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) (v : E) : unitPart g v = (homRatio g)⁻¹ • g v := by
  show homothety E (homRatioHom E g : ℝˣ)⁻¹ (g v) = _
  rw [homothety_apply, Units.val_inv_eq_inv_val, coe_homRatioHom]

theorem unitPart_mem_GU [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [Nontrivial E] (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) :
    unitPart g ∈ GU E := by
  rw [mem_GU, unitPart, map_mul, Units.val_mul, det_homothety, abs_mul]
  simp only [Units.val_inv_eq_inv_val, coe_homRatioHom, inv_pow, abs_inv, abs_pow]
  rw [abs_of_pos (homRatio_pos g), homRatio,
    Real.rpow_inv_natCast_pow (abs_nonneg _) Module.finrank_pos.ne']
  exact inv_mul_cancel₀ (absDet_pos g).ne'

section Decomposition

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [Nontrivial E]

theorem homRatio_homothety {c : ℝˣ} (hc : 0 < (c : ℝ)) : homRatio (homothety E c) = c := by
  rw [homRatio, det_homothety, abs_pow, abs_of_pos hc,
    Real.pow_rpow_inv_natCast hc.le Module.finrank_pos.ne']

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [Nontrivial E] in
theorem homRatio_of_mem_GU {u : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E} (hu : u ∈ GU E) : homRatio u = 1 := by
  rw [homRatio, mem_GU.1 hu, Real.one_rpow]

variable (E) in
/-- `g ↦ |det g|^{-1/n} g`, a homomorphism `GL(E) →* GU(E)`. -/
def unitPartHom : (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) →* GU E where
  toFun g := ⟨unitPart g, unitPart_mem_GU g⟩
  map_one' := by
    apply Subtype.ext; ext v
    simp [unitPart_apply, homRatio]
  map_mul' g h := by
    apply Subtype.ext; ext v
    simp only [unitPart_apply, Subgroup.coe_mul, LinearEquiv.mul_apply, homRatio_mul, map_smul,
      smul_smul, mul_inv]
    rw [mul_comm (homRatio g)⁻¹]

@[simp] theorem coe_unitPartHom (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) : (unitPartHom E g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) = unitPart g :=
  rfl

/-- **`GL(E)` is the direct product of `ℝ⁺` (the positive homotheties) and `GU(E)`** (p. 236):
`g ↦ (|det g|^{1/n}, |det g|^{-1/n} g)`, with inverse `(c, u) ↦ c • u`. -/
def glEquivProd : (E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) ≃* Units.posSubgroup ℝ × GU E where
  toFun g := (homRatioHom E g, unitPartHom E g)
  invFun p := homothety E (p.1 : ℝˣ) * (p.2 : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E)
  left_inv g := by
    ext v
    simp only [LinearEquiv.mul_apply, homothety_apply, coe_homRatioHom, coe_unitPartHom,
      unitPart_apply, smul_smul, mul_inv_cancel₀ (homRatio_pos g).ne', one_smul]
  right_inv p := by
    obtain ⟨⟨c, hc⟩, ⟨u, hu⟩⟩ := p
    have hc' : 0 < (c : ℝ) := (Units.mem_posSubgroup c).1 hc
    have hr : homRatio (homothety E c * u) = c := by
      rw [homRatio_mul, homRatio_homothety hc', homRatio_of_mem_GU hu, mul_one]
    refine Prod.ext (Subtype.ext (Units.ext ?_)) (Subtype.ext ?_)
    · exact hr
    · ext v
      simp only [coe_unitPartHom, unitPart_apply, hr, LinearEquiv.mul_apply, homothety_apply,
        smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hc'.ne', one_smul]
  map_mul' g h := by
    simp only [map_mul, Prod.mk_mul_mk]

@[simp] theorem glEquivProd_symm_apply (c : Units.posSubgroup ℝ) (u : GU E) :
    (glEquivProd (E := E)).symm (c, u) = homothety E (c : ℝˣ) * (u : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) := rfl

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] in
theorem homothety_injective : Function.Injective (homothety E) := by
  intro c d h
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_ne (0 : E)
  have := LinearEquiv.congr_fun h v
  simp only [homothety_apply] at this
  exact Units.ext (smul_left_injective ℝ hv this)

variable (E) in
/-- The positive homotheties form a subgroup isomorphic to `ℝ⁺` (« le sous-groupe, isomorphe à
$\R^+$, des homothéties positives »). -/
def posHomothetiesEquiv : Units.posSubgroup ℝ ≃* posHomotheties E :=
  (Units.posSubgroup ℝ).equivMapOfInjective (homothety E) homothety_injective

theorem ker_unitPartHom : (unitPartHom E).ker = posHomotheties E := by
  ext g
  rw [MonoidHom.mem_ker, mem_posHomotheties]
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine ⟨homRatio g, homRatio_pos g, fun v => ?_⟩
    have := LinearEquiv.congr_fun (congrArg Subtype.val h) v
    simp only [coe_unitPartHom, unitPart_apply, OneMemClass.coe_one, LinearEquiv.coe_one, id_eq] at this
    conv_rhs => rw [← this]
    rw [smul_smul, mul_inv_cancel₀ (homRatio_pos g).ne', one_smul]
  · rintro ⟨c, hc, hg⟩
    have hgc : g = homothety E (Units.mk0 c hc.ne') := by ext v; simp [hg]
    have hr : homRatio g = c := by rw [hgc, homRatio_homothety (by simpa using hc)]; rfl
    apply Subtype.ext; ext v
    simp only [coe_unitPartHom, unitPart_apply, hr, hg, smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hc.ne',
      one_smul, OneMemClass.coe_one, LinearEquiv.coe_one, id_eq]

theorem unitPartHom_surjective : Function.Surjective (unitPartHom E) := by
  rintro ⟨u, hu⟩
  refine ⟨u, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  ext v
  simp [unitPart_apply, homRatio_of_mem_GU hu]

variable (E) in
/-- **The isomorphism `i : GS(E) ≃* GU(E)`** (p. 236, « la projection de $GL(n, \R)$ sur son
quotient $GS(n-1, \R)$ définit donc un isomorphisme (noté $i$) de $GS(n-1, \R)$ sur
$GU(n, \R)$ »): `i(ḡ) = |det g|^{-1/n} g`. -/
def isoGU : GSE E ≃* GU E :=
  (QuotientGroup.quotientMulEquivOfEq ker_unitPartHom.symm).trans
    (QuotientGroup.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (unitPartHom E) unitPartHom_surjective)

@[simp] theorem isoGU_mk (g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) :
    (isoGU E (QuotientGroup.mk g) : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) = unitPart g := rfl

/-- The inverse of `i` is the restriction to `GU(E)` of the projection `GL(E) → GS(E)`. -/
theorem isoGU_symm_apply (u : GU E) : (isoGU E).symm u = QuotientGroup.mk (u : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) := by
  apply (isoGU E).injective
  rw [MulEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [isoGU_mk]
  ext v
  simp [unitPart_apply, homRatio_of_mem_GU u.2]

/-- `i(ḡ)` acts on `S(E)` as `ḡ` does. -/
theorem isoGU_smul (g : GSE E) (x : Sphere E) : (isoGU E g : E ≃ₗ[ℝ] E) • x = g • x := by
  conv_rhs => rw [← (isoGU E).symm_apply_apply g, isoGU_symm_apply]
  rfl

end Decomposition

end Unimodular

/-! ### The paper's indexing; `GA(n, ℝ)` -/

section Indexing

/-- **`GL(n, ℝ)`**, « le groupe des automorphismes de l'espace vectoriel $\R^n$ ». -/
abbrev GLR (n : ℕ) : Type := (Fin n → ℝ) ≃ₗ[ℝ] (Fin n → ℝ)

/-- **`GA(n, ℝ)`**, « le groupe des automorphismes de la structure d'espace affin de $\R^n$ »:
Mathlib's `AffineEquiv`, i.e. the bijections affine in the sense of Déf. 2 with `l'` linear
(`Benzecri.IsAffine`, the reading of DEC-114; `GAR.isAffine`, `GAR.exists_eq_of_isAffine`). -/
abbrev GAR (n : ℕ) : Type := (Fin n → ℝ) ≃ᵃ[ℝ] (Fin n → ℝ)

/-- **`GU(n, ℝ)`**: `|det| = 1`. -/
abbrev GUR (n : ℕ) : Subgroup (GLR n) := GU (Fin n → ℝ)

/-- **`GS(m, ℝ) = GL(m+1, ℝ)/ℝ⁺`**, acting on `S m = S(ℝᵐ⁺¹)` (Benzécri's `GS(n−1, ℝ)` on
`S(n−1)`, with `m = n − 1`). -/
abbrev GSR (m : ℕ) : Type := GSE (Fin (m + 1) → ℝ)

example (m : ℕ) : MulAction (GSR m) (S m) := inferInstance
example (m : ℕ) : ContinuousConstSMul (GSR m) (S m) := inferInstance
example (m : ℕ) : IsAnalyticAction (GSR m) (S m) := inferInstance

/-- **`i : GS(m, ℝ) ≃* GU(m+1, ℝ)`**. -/
def isoGUR (m : ℕ) : GSR m ≃* GUR (m + 1) := isoGU _

variable {n : ℕ}

/-- The translation by `v`, an element of `GA(n, ℝ)`. -/
def GAR.translation (v : Fin n → ℝ) : GAR n := AffineEquiv.constVAdd ℝ (Fin n → ℝ) v

/-- Every element of `GA(n, ℝ)` is a linear automorphism followed by a translation. -/
theorem GAR.eq_translation_mul_linear (f : GAR n) :
    f = GAR.translation (f 0) * f.linear.toAffineEquiv := by
  ext x : 1
  rw [AffineEquiv.coe_mul, Function.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_toAffineEquiv, GAR.translation,
    AffineEquiv.constVAdd_apply, vadd_eq_add]
  have := f.map_vadd 0 x
  simp only [vadd_eq_add, add_zero] at this
  rw [this, add_comm]

/-- **`GA(n, ℝ)` is generated by `GL(n, ℝ)` and the translations** (p. 236). -/
theorem closure_linear_union_translations :
    Subgroup.closure (range (fun g : GLR n => g.toAffineEquiv) ∪ range GAR.translation) = ⊤ := by
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  intro f _
  rw [GAR.eq_translation_mul_linear f]
  exact Subgroup.mul_mem _ (Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨_, rfl⟩))
    (Subgroup.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨_, rfl⟩))

/-- Every element of `GA(n, ℝ)` is affine in the sense of Déf. 2 (`Benzecri.IsAffine`). -/
theorem GAR.isAffine (f : GAR n) : IsAffine ℝ f :=
  isAffine_of_affineMap f.toAffineMap

/-- **`GA(n, ℝ)` is the group of automorphisms of the affine structure of Déf. 2**: a bijection of
`ℝⁿ` that is affine in the sense of `Benzecri.IsAffine` is an element of `GA(n, ℝ)`. -/
theorem GAR.exists_eq_of_isAffine {f : (Fin n → ℝ) → (Fin n → ℝ)} (hf : IsAffine ℝ f)
    (hb : Function.Bijective f) : ∃ g : GAR n, ⇑g = f := by
  obtain ⟨φ, rfl⟩ := (isAffine_iff ℝ f).1 hf
  exact ⟨AffineEquiv.ofBijective hb, rfl⟩

/-- Every element of `GA(n, ℝ)` acts on `ℝⁿ` by a homeomorphism (it is continuous, as is its
inverse). -/
theorem GAR.continuous (f : GAR n) : Continuous f := f.continuous_of_finiteDimensional

end Indexing

end Benzecri
